# Genesis Dashboard — production env template (T-D-011 sprint_10).
#
# Copy to `.env.production` for a local prod build OR set these in the
# Vercel project's Environment Variables. NEVER commit the real values.
#
# Hard rule from the task brief:
#   "Do not commit real values into .env.production.example (placeholders
#   only). Do not hardcode bearer tokens; use session/localStorage + env
#   var pattern only."
#
# ----------------------------------------------------------------------
# WHY THESE VARS HAVE NO `NEXT_PUBLIC_` PREFIX (T-D-011 fix)
# ----------------------------------------------------------------------
#
# Sprint_9 (T-D-010) shipped with `NEXT_PUBLIC_DASHBOARD_API_TOKEN` —
# which Vercel inlines into every browser bundle. The User caught a
# 401 on the live `/workshop` flow because the deployed Vercel build
# had NEXT_PUBLIC_DASHBOARD_API_URL set but no NEXT_PUBLIC_TOKEN
# (correctly — you can't safely put a secret in NEXT_PUBLIC_*).
#
# T-D-011 sprint_10 introduces `dashboard/app/api/proxy/[...path]/route.ts`,
# a same-origin Next.js server route that injects the bearer token in the
# Vercel server runtime. The browser only ever calls `/api/proxy/...` —
# the token never leaves Vercel's server. Hence the env vars below carry
# NO `NEXT_PUBLIC_` prefix; that is intentional and required for security.
#
# ----------------------------------------------------------------------
# REQUIRED — server-side proxy (T-D-011)
# ----------------------------------------------------------------------

# Base URL of the Track B FastAPI control plane (agent.server.main).
# Examples:
#   - Local dev   →  http://localhost:8000
#   - Railway     →  https://genesis-agent.up.railway.app
#   - Fly.io      →  https://genesis-agent.fly.dev
#
# Read by `dashboard/app/api/proxy/[...path]/route.ts` ONLY (server-side).
# Adding `NEXT_PUBLIC_` to this name would still work but the URL would
# leak into the browser bundle — keep it server-only.
DASHBOARD_API_URL=https://example.invalid

# Bearer token the proxy injects on every forwarded request. NEVER
# duplicate this into `NEXT_PUBLIC_*` — doing so would expose it to every
# visitor's browser, defeating the entire proxy model.
#
# Generate with `openssl rand -hex 32` and store in Vercel's Environment
# Variables (Production scope). Rotate by updating both Vercel and the
# Track B backend simultaneously.
DASHBOARD_API_TOKEN=replace-me-with-a-32-byte-hex-secret

# ----------------------------------------------------------------------
# OPTIONAL — local-dev escape hatch
# ----------------------------------------------------------------------

# Set this to bypass the proxy and have the browser talk directly to the
# upstream FastAPI (useful when running both Next.js + FastAPI locally).
# DO NOT set this in production — it pulls the token out of the browser's
# localStorage instead of the server-side env, which is fine for local
# dev but re-introduces the very leakage T-D-011 closed.
#
# Example for local dev only:
#   NEXT_PUBLIC_DASHBOARD_API_URL_OVERRIDE=http://localhost:8000
# NEXT_PUBLIC_DASHBOARD_API_URL_OVERRIDE=

# ----------------------------------------------------------------------
# OPTIONAL — sprint_4–8 pipeline / playback
# ----------------------------------------------------------------------

# Live WebSocket bridge URL (sprint_4–8 pipeline; see lib/ws-client.ts).
# Distinct from the FastAPI control-plane SSE — the WS carries vitals +
# consciousness frames; the SSE carries decisions / reflections / proposals.
# NEXT_PUBLIC_WS_URL=wss://example.invalid/ws

# Optional override for the playback fixture path (sprint_4 demo arc).
# NEXT_PUBLIC_PLAYBACK_FIXTURE=/playback/genesis_demo_arc.v1.json
